            <ArticleTitle>An unusual cause of foot pain in a child: osteochondrosis of the intermediate cuneiform.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>474-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.jfas.2009.02.010</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="UNLABELLED">Osteochondrosis of the intermediate cuneiform is a rare entity that may cause foot pain and limping in children. We report a case of osteochondrosis of the intermediate cuneiform in a child who underwent a spontaneous recovery after conservative treatment.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="LEVEL OF CLINICAL EVIDENCE" NlmCategory="METHODS">4.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
